{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Elohim chanced upon Balaam.</b> The world asks: why did the Holy One, blessed be He, go to meet Balaam, but did not go to meet Moses our master, peace be upon him — rather He called him, as it is written: ויקרא אל משה? One may say: this is a parable to a king who sits in his palace. A certain leper comes and calls at the gate, wanting to speak with the king. They came and told the king. The king said: Do not let him enter, lest he defile my palace; rather, I will go speak with him outside. But when his beloved wants to speak with him, he does not move from his place, and lets him come into his inner chambers and speaks with him."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:00.414866635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}